I remember CRT nights
Fans humming under bedroom lights
Every command could change the world
Every boot felt like a brand-new door

We grew up, the wonder disappeared
Then I heard that old machine again

Turn it on again
Let the old sparks fly
Put tomorrow on the screen
With the past still burning bright
Build it, break it, learn it
Make the whole thing mine
Silicon Siren riding shotgun
With an agent by my side

No walled garden, velvet rope
Just an open door and somewhere to go
From beige-box dreams to Quattro glow
The future feels like something I know

Not nostalgia
Not retreat
Just the joy we used to seek

Turn it on again
Omarchy
Make computers ours again